// ============================================================ styles

// Styles: typography, spacing and composition. No colour appears here — a style
// only ever names semantic palette tokens, which is what lets any style pair
// with any palette.
//
// Every size is a multiple of the body size, so `text-size` scales the whole
// hierarchy coherently instead of resizing one font.

// Newsreader carries an optical-size axis, so Typst registers it under this
// name. Internal only: users select the `academic` style, never the family.
#let SERIF-TEXT = "Newsreader 16pt"

